sk_type` is visible, correct, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]identically styled everywhere its triage or wake gate appears — the[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]ACE toast, the notification row, the gate detail pane, the gate [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]review modal, the Markdown preview, and the mobile wire — carried [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]as presentation frozen into the gate at creation time, so no render[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]path reads the task-type registry and no surface can disagree with [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]another.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_type_gate_presentation.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/task_type_gate_presentation.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-pq[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-pq/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A gate may declare one subject chip[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]chip[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]chip: add the generic `presentation.chip` field (glyph, label, optional [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]color), normalize and protect it like `panel_icon`, project it into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notification `action_data`, and add the tolerant zero-I/O reader every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]render surface uses.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Frozen task-type presentation[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]freeze[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chip[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]freeze: add the module that resolves one task type into a frozen glyph, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]human name, accent, and ordered required-field facts at gate-creation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]time, plus the strict parser, chip projection, note line, and Markdown [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fact every later phase renders from.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The toast and the notification row[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]dense[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chip[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]dense: give TaskTriage and BeadSnooze their own toast branch with the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]chip, the typed detail line, and warning severity, and render the chip [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glyph on notification rows.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The gate detail pane and the gate review modal[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]detail[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chip[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]detail: render the declared chip as its own row in the notification [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]modal's gate pane and in the custom gate review modal's header, from [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`action_data` only.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task bead gates declare their type[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gates[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chip, freeze[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gates: freeze the task-type display block into the TaskTriage and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]BeadSnooze payloads, declare the chip, the typed note line, and the type[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tag, add the `**Task type:**` preview fact, and rebuild the whole [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation in kind validation instead of hand-checking its fields.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A pending gate refreshes when its type presentation changes[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]refresh[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gates[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refresh: fold the frozen display block into the reconciler's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation fingerprint and bump the presentation format version so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pending gates carrying the old, typeless presentation are replaced.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prove it end to end and document it[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]prove[dim] · [dim][/dim]after dense, detail, gates, refresh[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prove: add the one end-to-end test that drives a real typed gate through[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every surface, refresh and extend the PNG snapshots, and document the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]chip field and the typed gate surfaces.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-pq","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-pq.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-42c55788d95808cc104f72c79da2461e","started_at":"2026-08-18T13:39:10.361687+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1787064159,"sha":"5df9ed7600535b957e4826c1797b5c9d0dc57114","subject":"feat(tui): show task-type chips on bead-gate toasts and rows"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"8d821fefa21a9674ca6fb2699913fc6f69aa7ffbe119df68e032bebc079ddb98","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-pq.3/chat.md","size_bytes":5512},"commits":{"digest":"5aaa7376264255f8db6d79fac35b49a58111d6d7a22953a4892058844a9a69ff","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-pq.3/commits.json","size_bytes":238},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agen